(SSH  client)  is a program for logging into a remote machine and
for executing commands on a remote machine.  It  is  intended  to
provide  secure  encrypted  communications  between two untrusted
hosts over an insecure network.  X11 connections,  arbitrary  TCP
ports  and sockets can also be forwarded over the secure channel.
